@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@username = {{$dotenv AUTH_TEST_USERNAME}}
@password = {{$dotenv AUTH_TEST_PASSWORD}}

### Open: login returns an access token and a one-time refresh token
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

###

@accessToken = {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@refreshToken = {{login.response.body.$.refreshToken}}

### JWT: access token authenticates the session
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### JWT: inspect effective RBAC permissions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### Open: rotate refresh token; the old refresh token must not be reused
# @name refreshed
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/refresh
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

###

@rotatedAccessToken = {{refreshed.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@rotatedRefreshToken = {{refreshed.response.body.$.refreshToken}}

### JWT: list active and revoked sessions without exposing token hashes
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{rotatedAccessToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### Open: revoke the current refresh session
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{rotatedRefreshToken}}"
}

###

### JWT + RBAC: admin-only endpoint is denied to AUTH_TESTER (expect 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/usuarios
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Accept: application/json
